21,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The earth-movers are worried about clay and slippage, but small work is fine. Also, we can't hoard the center or main gate without closing them.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,May,,"The habitat fund only pays for plants and water, not buildings. Also, planted areas are costing us triple what hard surfaces do every year.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The eastern avenue trees mostly died from lack of water, but the old overflow basin is still in perfect shape after eight years.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"Our staff has dropped from eighteen to seven. We buy in specialist water care, but we have volunteers for habitats and youth sports.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"People mostly stick to firm ground to reach the tram. Plus, drainage callouts are doubling and the heat in the open areas is intense.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, if people stay on firm ground, does that mean we should avoid soft paths in the center?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, if we have so few staff, can we really afford the high upkeep of planted areas I found?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, that is a very good point. My findings show that without proper aftercare, the plants just die anyway.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, it is a struggle. We rely on contractors for the specialized stuff, which is expensive.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, exactly. The margins are ignored. We need something that handles the flow and the heat.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shizue, you mentioned the overflow basin is still good. Does that mean water-based projects last longer?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, if the heat is that bad, maybe we need more shade, but I'm terrified of the long-term maintenance costs.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Shizue,,It seems the structural water works were more successful than the decorative planting.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, if the drainage is failing, a plan that ignores the culverts will just lead to more callouts.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Precisely. We need a solution that works with the water, not against it.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Minato,,I'm just worried about the clay. Big digs might cause a mess.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,May,,"We must prioritize the fund's terms. If it doesn't pay for the paving, we're paying for it twice.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us look for something durable and simple.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Victoria,,And something the remaining staff or volunteers can actually manage.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,pass,Shunichi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
45,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
