49,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Minato,,"The options are A: Woodland Walk, B: Market Plaza, C: Sports Terraces, and D: Wetland Restoration. I'm worried about the digging for B and C.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,May,,"A and D fit the habitat fund, but A's upkeep will be a nightmare. B and C are too expensive to maintain.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Shizue,,A is risky; remember the eastern avenue trees. D's ponds are like the overflow basin—they last.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Victoria,,D uses the habitat volunteers. C uses the sports volunteers. But D solves the drainage issues Shunichi mentioned.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,A and B ignore the heat and drainage. C is just more hard surface for the tram-commuters. D is the most rational.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, would the Wetland Restoration require too much heavy earth-moving?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, would the volunteers be enough to keep the costs down for the wetlands?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, it's more about reshaping than massive excavation. It feels more natural for the site.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, yes, the habitat group is already active upriver. They are a reliable resource.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"D addresses the heat, the drainage, and the fund's restrictions. It's the only one that hits every mark.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Minato,,I think D is the safest for the ground.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,May,,It's the only one that doesn't bankrupt us in three years. I vote D.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I vote for D. It is a gentle and lasting choice.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. D is manageable with our current rota. I vote D.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I vote D. It's the only plan that respects the actual behavior of the site.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote D too!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
